Package: lt
Type: Package
Title: Lightweight Tables via JSON Specs and JavaScript
Version: 0.4.17
Authors@R: person('Yihui', 'Xie', email = 'xie@yihui.name', role = c('aut', 'cre', 'cph'),
    comment = c(ORCID = '0000-0003-0645-5666', URL = 'https://yihui.org'))
Description: A lightweight grammar of tables. Build a table by declaring a JSON
    spec (titles, spanners, row groups, footnotes, formatting functions, etc.); a tiny
    vanilla JavaScript runtime builds the HTML table from the spec on page
    load. Tables can optionally be made interactive (sorting, searching,
    filtering, pagination, and expandable row detail) via a separate extension
    loaded only when requested. No 'sass', no 'V8', no 'htmlwidgets' — just base
    R and 'xfun' ('htmltools' is used only for the optional Shiny binding and
    for embedding tables in other HTML output).
